WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.330
- Please welcome, John Kanell!

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:04.615
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:00:04.615 --> 00:00:06.600
- [John] Thank you for having me.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.700
- Okay, I love your story.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.060
You became a teacher.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:15.420
You were a good teacher.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:18.350
- [John] Thank you.
- But something inside of you

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:21.520
felt another path that you would foster

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.690
by cooking in your off-hours
and feeding your passion.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.800
But what made it take
over into pole position?

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.720
- I mean, there's two
things happening here.

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:30.980
My mom is from Mexico

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.380
and she instilled a
love of education in me,

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:35.550
it's part of why I became a teacher.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:37.810
But she also had a love of cooking

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:39.210
and exploring flavors

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.100
and just trying things
out and being adventurous,

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.640
and I grew up with her in the kitchen.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:45.660
So even though I was a
math and science teacher

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:46.630
and I loved it,

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:49.370
I still had a passion for
cooking that I nurtured

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:51.740
and it really kept me going.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:53.680
But when my husband, Brian, and I decided

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:55.120
we wanted to have a family.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.260
- [Drew] And you guys live on a farm.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:57.370
- We live on a farm now.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:59.530
And like, we're both from LA.

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:01.620
Now we live on this farm in Connecticut.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.790
And so we wanted to have kids

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:05.770
and I knew I wanted to
be home more with them.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:08.130
So I took my love of
teaching and my love of food

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:09.490
and I created Preppy Kitchen

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:11.610
where I get to be home with the kids,

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:14.270
but I can also teach people
how to make delicious food

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:15.670
and have fun in the kitchen.

00:01:16.835 --> 00:01:19.350
(audience clapping)

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:21.963
- And your husband,
Brian, is in the audience.

00:01:21.963 --> 00:01:23.223
- Yes, yes, he is.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:28.710
- What's it like to live with
someone who can really cook?

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:32.480
- Well, I'm incredibly well
fed, as you may imagine.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:33.710
I like to consider myself

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:35.800
the chief tasting officer
of Preppy Kitchen.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:36.633
So it's fun.

00:01:36.633 --> 00:01:39.850
- I love that you call yourself
the chief tasting officer.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:40.750
- I can't cook anything.

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:42.730
So I would starve to death without John.

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:44.980
- Okay, so your upcoming
book that I've been searching

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:47.520
high and low for is coming out in October

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:50.280
and it is my pick for Cookbook Club.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:51.800
What can we expect?

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:54.400
- Well, we're all from LA, right?

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:55.233
- Yes.

00:01:55.233 --> 00:01:57.367
- And when we moved to
Connecticut, I was like,

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:59.650
"I love this, this is amazing."

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:01.560
Like the summer was just magical

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.400
with like the plants breathing
and you can just feel it.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:05.660
- You appreciate it.
- Yeah.

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:09.040
- So the seasons just affect
every part of your life.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:10.640
- And that's a big part of your cookbook.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:13.010
- And we arranged all the
recipes by the seasons,

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:15.570
because I have different
needs in the winter.

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:19.040
I wanna have cozy, just hearty,
delicious food like this.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:20.460
- [Drew] And different stuff available.

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:21.293
- [John] Yeah.

00:02:21.293 --> 00:02:23.842
(upbeat music)

